{
  "challenges": [
    {
      "publicId": "chal_coding_pdp_182",
      "name": "partition-backfills",
      "type": "mini_coding",
      "title": "Recompute commission one business day at a time",
      "description": "`fact_commission` holds the commission per restaurant per business day (Ho Chi Minh City time, UTC+7) that the monthly invoices read. After a rate fix, the first October backfill appended rows and doubled October, and the nightly job loaded \"today in UTC\", missing orders placed after midnight local time. The editor holds `pipelines/commission.py` with its key pieces missing, each marked by a `# [ ]` line; some pieces are wrong on purpose. Fill every line so that `run_day` recomputes exactly one business day (18% of the summed subtotal) and gives the same rows when run again, `backfill` runs every day from start to end with both ends included, oldest first, and `nightly` recomputes the `lookback` business days before the run date, so late orders land in their own day. Run executes the test's steps against SQLite and prints the days each step processed and the final fact table.",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "outcomes": [
        "orchestration"
      ],
      "points": 30,
      "hints": [
        "Pick one order placed at 06:30 in Ho Chi Minh City and one at 01:00: which business day owns each, and what happens to the fact table when the same day is processed twice?",
        "Look at converting a local midnight to UTC with `datetime` and `timedelta`, `DELETE` then `INSERT` for one partition inside one transaction, and a `while` loop over `date` objects with an inclusive end.",
        "Rebuilding daily courier payouts per business day in Jakarta (UTC+7): `start = datetime.fromisoformat(day) - timedelta(hours=7)`, then in one transaction `DELETE FROM payouts WHERE day = ?` and `INSERT INTO payouts SELECT ?, courier_id, SUM(fee) FROM deliveries WHERE delivered_at >= ? AND delivered_at < ? GROUP BY courier_id`; a backfill loops `while d <= end_date`."
      ],
      "coding": {
        "language": "python",
        "filePath": "pipelines/commission.py",
        "executionMode": "stdio",
        "timeLimitMs": 3000,
        "memoryLimitMb": 128,
        "scoringMode": "all_or_nothing",
        "maxAttempts": null
      },
